8275862068966, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The ECG pattern is suggestive of Mobitz type II AV block due to consistent PR intervals with intermittently blocked beats, which differentiates from sinus bradycardia.", "ECG findings support Mobitz II AV block over sinus bradycardia based on consistent PR intervals with dropped beats."], "evidence_against": ["Normal vital signs and youth status create a weak challenge to intrinsic AV pathophysiology as the primary diagnosis, maintaining neutrality for other branches.", "Normal QRS morphology argues against intrinsic AV structural disease, indirectly supporting reactive arrhythmia (B3)"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are there episodes of syncope or near-syncope?", "Does the patient have a family history of conduction disorders?", "Are the palpitations associated with positional changes or exercise?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG: PR interval consistency across beats (first degree vs. variable blocks)", "ECG: Presence of bundle branch block patterns (Mobitz I vs. II)", "ECG: Evidence of complete AV dissociation (third degree block)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Sinus Rhythm Abnormality", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "confirmed", "prior": 0.5779816513761468, "posterior": 0.4827586206896552, "danger": 0.1, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The presence of regular P-P intervals supports a sinus origin of rhythm abnormalities, aligning with the high likelihood of primary sinus bradycardia in an otherwise healthy young woman."], "evidence_against": ["The ECG pattern is suggestive of Mobitz type II AV block due to consistent PR intervals with intermittently blocked beats, which differentiates from sinus bradycardia.", "ECG findings support Mobitz II AV block over sinus bradycardia based on consistent PR intervals with dropped beats."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is the patient a competitive athlete?", "Are there symptoms of hypoperfusion?", "Is the bradycardia constant or intermittent?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG: Confirmation of sinus node morphology without conduction delay", "ECG: Evidence of sinus pauses or sinoatrial blocks"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Reactive Arrhythmia with Caffeine Sensitivity", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.09174311926605505, "posterior": 0.1724137931034483, "danger": 0.0, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Normal QRS morphology argues against intrinsic AV structural disease, indirectly supporting reactive arrhythmia (B3)"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Exact timing of palpitations relative to caffeine intake", "Does symptom severity correlate with specific caffeine sources (coffee vs. energy drinks)?", "Any concurrent stress or anxiety symptoms?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG: Evidence of tachycardia-bradycardia syndrome patterns", "ECG: Non-specific T-wave changes or sinusoidal pattern (pre-excitation)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "First Degree Atrioventricular Block", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.05387931034482758, "posterior": 0.05387931034482758, "danger": 0.1, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are there episodes of syncope without dropped QRS complexes?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG: PR interval prolongation across all beats (consistent ≥ 200ms without intermittent dropping)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Second Degree Atrioventricular Block (Mobitz Type I - Wenckebach)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16163793103448273, "posterior": 0.16163793103448273, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are palpitations associated with progressive PR interval prolongation before dropped beats?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG: Progressive PR interval lengthening before non-conducted P waves"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Second Degree Atrioventricular Block (Mobitz Type II - Non-Wenckebach)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.10775862068965517, "posterior": 0.10775862068965517, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Do symptoms occur in fixed cycles rather than varying PR intervals?"], "reques